        1
      ],
      "blind_answer": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "blind_working": "H2O is bent, so its bond dipoles do not cancel. CO2 (linear), BF3 (trigonal planar) and CCl4 (tetrahedral) are symmetric, so their bond dipoles cancel and the net moment is zero."
    },
    {
