      ],
      "blind_answer": 3,
      "confidence": "high",
      "blind_working": "In o-nitrophenol, the -OH and -NO2 groups are adjacent, so they form an H-bond within the same molecule (a chelate ring). p-Nitrophenol, acetic acid dimers and ethanol all H-bond between molecules."
    },
    {
      "q_id": "neet_che_u03_t16_2",
      "published": true,
      "reason": null,
      "manual_approved": false,
      "our_answer": [
        3
      ],
      "blind_answer": 3,
      "confidence": "high",
      "blind_working": "Observed boiling points are H2O 373 K, HF about 293 K and NH3 about 240 K. Water forms more H-bonds per molecule (two H atoms and two lone pairs), so the order is H2O > HF > NH3."
    },
    {
      "q_id": "neet_che_u03_t16_3",
      "published": true,
      "reason": null,
      "manual_approved": false,
      "our_answer": [
        3
      ],
      "blind_answer": 3,
      "confidence": "high",
      "blind_working": "In ice, H-bonding fixes each molecule in a tetrahedral open cage with empty spaces. This makes ice less dense than liquid water, so it floats."
    },
    {
      "q_id": "neet_che_u03_t16_4",
      "published": true,
      "reason": null,
